From 57dbb4025fac755c06611afdcc3806ad92398850 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 21:30:18 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Wallguard: Unbreak by device, stored lists kept current, and
 the page in tabs (102.8 line)

- Unbreak keeps an hour of blocked lookups (it kept the last 500 for all devices), matches a
  device by its MAC or its current addresses, leaves out names that are allowed now, and shows a
  CNAME block as "<asked> (blocked via <listed>)". After Allow the row says it takes effect for
  new lookups.
- Lists kept on a USB store: a list downloaded before the store was mounted stayed in RAM while
  the store kept the older copy, so every rebuild rejected the stored copies. The newest copy is
  used and moved to the store, checked after the copy.
- A rebuild that was skipped, or used fewer lists than chosen, is reported on the page.
- The page is in five tabs: Overview (Fix a device, Pause with a 10-minute choice, Why?, counters,
  warnings), Lists, Rules, Devices (one row per device: profile, blocked lookups in the last 15
  minutes, Fix and Pause; it replaces the assignment table) and Activity (live view with a device
  filter, statistics). New query: blocked lookups per device for the last 1 to 60 minutes.
- Texts in all 25 language packs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
